+#     - Input is still a 29x29 separator grid with 7x7 cells of size 3x3.
+#     - Majority/minority cell interiors are built exactly as in the seed:
+#       the minority interior uses one dominant color whose 3x3 support is the
+#       higher-level mask.
+#     - The input still shows only a strict subset of minority cells, but their
+#       absolute placement is now only a clue source, not the destination.
+#       They are intentionally drawn at a legal non-central offset.
+#     - Solver extracts the minority texture and its boolean mask, ignores the
+#       clue offset, centers the enlarged 3x3 cell block on the 7x7 lattice, and
+#       returns only that 3x3 block with its outer divider frame.
+#   trace_example:
+#     - Seed behavior:
+#       1. Read the odd cell texture.
+#       2. Treat its dominant-color pixels as a 3x3 stencil.
+#       3. Use the shown minority-cell coordinates to locate that stencil on the
+#          board.
+#       4. Fill the full board at that located block and return the whole board.
+#     - Combo behavior:
+#       1. Steps 1-2 are unchanged.
+#       2. The shown minority cells may sit at offset (0,4), (4,1), etc., but
+#          that offset is ignored when constructing the answer.
+#       3. The 3x3 enlarged block is rendered at the centered offset
+#          ((7-3)//2, (7-3)//2) = (2,2).
+#       4. Only the centered 3x3 block is returned, so the output is always the
+#          compact 13x13 mini-grid corresponding to the centered enlargement.
+#     - Difference:
+#       D3 removes the old anchoring assumption; D9 removes the untouched outer
+#       board. The user-visible effect is that off-center clues generate the
+#       same centered local answer.
+#   complexity_guardrails:
+#     - Preserve the original 4-color role system and LR-symmetric 3x3 pattern
+#       family so the task remains recognizably b99e7126.
+#     - Keep the minority active count at 6-7 and the shown clue count at 3-4,
+#       so the minority texture is visually rich and still clearly rarer than
+#       the majority texture.
